      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I'm Dr. Smith. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S005",
      "patient_response": "Hello, Dr. Smith. Well, I... I came in because I just can’t seem to get anything in order anymore. It's getting so bad. Like, my kitchen table right now? It is completely covered with my husband’s appointment papers. Frank has been seeing a new cardiologist—Dr. Miller, over on 4th street? Such a nice man, but his waiting room is always freezing. I always tell Frank to bring a sweater, but does he listen? \n\nAnyway, Frank's papers are there, along with all these church flyers. I usually help with the spring bazaar, I make a lovely lemon pound cake, though I couldn't find decent lemons at the grocery store this week... they were all so hard. Oh, and the senior-center notes are piled up there too, and just... half-finished lists everywhere. I sit down at that table, and I look at it all, and I just don't know which thing to do first. I just sit there. And then I look at the clock and the whole entire day is gone. I just don't know where the time goes.",
