    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you find yourself unable to start those tasks, is it because you feel overwhelmed by the clutter, or is it because you are having trouble remembering what those papers are for?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "I'm not really sure... I mean, I know what the papers are, mostly. Like Frank's medical bills, I know those are for him. He really shouldn't be eating so much salt with his heart the way it is, but he just loves those big soft pretzels. You know, the kind they sell at the mall? We used to get them all the time when the girls were little and we'd go back-to-school shopping. The mall used to be so lovely back then. Now half the stores are just boarded up. It’s such a shame, really. I needed to buy a new pair of walking shoes last month and I had to drive all the way out to the county line just to find a place that sells decent arch support. The salesman was very young, didn't know a thing about proper sizing, kept trying to put me in these neon pink sneakers... \n\nBut, oh dear, what was your question? I'm sorry. The papers on the table? I just... I look at it all and I really don't know why I can't start. I just don't know.",
