    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Beyond the difficulty with your tasks, have you been feeling down, sad, or hopeless lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Sad? Oh, no, I don't think so. I mean, I get terribly frustrated with myself, but I wouldn't say hopeless. Now, my neighbor Doris, she gets very down. She was just telling me over the fence on Tuesday... or was it Wednesday? No, Tuesday, because Tuesday is when the street sweeper comes by. They make such a terrible racket, and honestly, they don't even really pick up the leaves. \n\nThe big oak tree in our front yard drops leaves all year round, it seems. Frank used to rake them every single weekend, but his back just can't take it anymore. We tried hiring the Henderson boy from down the street to do it, but teenagers these days, they just stare at their phones. I saw him standing right in the middle of the lawn, rake in one hand, just tapping away on that little screen with his thumb. I don't even know what they look at on those things all day long. My granddaughter showed me how to look at pictures of recipes on my iPad, which is nice, I suppose, but the screen gets so smudgy with fingerprints. I tried wiping it with a paper towel and Frank said I was going to scratch the glass... \n\nOh, I'm sorry. Did I even answer your question? I just get to talking and my mind goes right out the window. What did you ask me?",
