    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you always struggled with this kind of disorganization and difficulty getting started on tasks since you were much younger, or is this a new problem that has developed more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, heavens, no, it's not new at all. It’s always been this way. Even when I was just a little girl, my teachers would write on my report cards that I was a bright child but just so careless. I was always forgetting my reading books or leaving my homework at home, and they constantly had to remind me to finish my seatwork before I was ever allowed to go outside for recess. \n\nWe had the most wonderful playground at my elementary school, though. It had one of those giant metal merry-go-rounds. You just don't see those anymore, they say they're too dangerous for children now. My brother Tommy flew right off one once and tore a huge hole in the knee of his brand new corduroy pants. My mother was just livid because she had just bought them from the Sears Roebuck catalog. Oh, the Sears catalog... we used to wait for the big Christmas wish book to arrive in the mail and we'd sit on the rug and circle all the toys we wanted with a red crayon. I think I still have a tin of Tommy's old crayons somewhere up in the attic. Or maybe it's down in the basement? Though the basement gets terribly damp in the spring, I keep telling Frank we need to have a plumber look at the pipes down there before all our old photo boxes get ruined... \n\nOh dear. I've done it again, haven't I? Did that answer your question about the pipes, or... what were we talking about?",
